{"chunk_id": "/Users/anwarh/Desktop/IBM/Automation/Agent/work_knowledge_agent/data/raw/work_IBM/main-EST-Users-Guide/EST-User-Guide-main/Automation/SE_Tools/EST_Tools/reit/io/IOINJ/README.md::chunk-0007-ec05f9899d9486c3", "source_file": "/Users/anwarh/Desktop/IBM/Automation/Agent/work_knowledge_agent/data/raw/work_IBM/main-EST-Users-Guide/EST-User-Guide-main/Automation/SE_Tools/EST_Tools/reit/io/IOINJ/README.md", "section_heading": "Functions", "project": "work_knowledge_agent", "machine": "unknown", "component": "unknown", "mode": "unknown", "doc_type": "readme", "date": "2026-07-04", "owner": "unknown", "tags": ["ingested", "md"], "confidentiality_level": "internal", "extracted_commands": [], "extracted_errors": ["The print function outputs content of an error file to the console. The user specifies the error file contents to be printed using the -f option. The outputted content of which includes populated requirements and error data from other files that correspond to the error file.", "The query function queries the system for connected hardware. This can be done as a general query or an error file can be provided by the user using the -f option to query for hardware that meets the requiements for an individual error."], "doc_type_confidence": 0.9, "section_heading_confidence": 0.9, "metadata_confidence": 0.9, "provenance": {"loader_version": "2.0.0", "chunker_version": "2.0.0", "extractor_version": "2.0.0", "ingested_at": "2026-07-04T02:09:57.683132+00:00", "content_hash": "1978caa329cba6cc592d8e04afb2f0fb5e66ac261c0f9fd24f85a4b831270264", "loader_route": ".md"}}
{"chunk_id": "/Users/anwarh/Desktop/IBM/Automation/Agent/work_knowledge_agent/data/raw/work_IBM/main-EST-Users-Guide/EST-User-Guide-main/Automation/SE_Tools/EST_Tools/reit/io/IOINJ/README.md::chunk-0008-ef6b1ede8a5c61c2", "source_file": "/Users/anwarh/Desktop/IBM/Automation/Agent/work_knowledge_agent/data/raw/work_IBM/main-EST-Users-Guide/EST-User-Guide-main/Automation/SE_Tools/EST_Tools/reit/io/IOINJ/README.md", "section_heading": "untitled-section", "project": "work_knowledge_agent", "machine": "unknown", "component": "unknown", "mode": "unknown", "doc_type": "readme", "date": "2026-07-04", "owner": "unknown", "tags": ["ingested", "md"], "confidentiality_level": "internal", "extracted_commands": [], "extracted_errors": ["ry for hardware that meets the requiements for an individual error.", "The inject function is used for executing error injects. Users provide an error file using the -f option and the tool will create a loop of injects to perform based on the data given within the testcase, requirements, and error_data corresponding to that error. Users can also provide one or more indexes using the -e option which determines what variable sets defined in the error data to use. These variable sets determine the values that are filled within the procedures when generating the inject loop. The inject loop will contain an inject for each combination of variable sets and hwa/pchid/vchid given."], "doc_type_confidence": 0.9, "section_heading_confidence": 0.3, "metadata_confidence": 0.3, "provenance": {"loader_version": "2.0.0", "chunker_version": "2.0.0", "extractor_version": "2.0.0", "ingested_at": "2026-07-04T02:09:57.683176+00:00", "content_hash": "1978caa329cba6cc592d8e04afb2f0fb5e66ac261c0f9fd24f85a4b831270264", "loader_route": ".md"}, "metadata_validation_flags": ["metadata_confidence_below_threshold", "missing_section_heading"]}
